# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Mechanical-before-agentic, landed 2026-07-31.
#
# Every rung of the dispatch CHECKPOINT chose WHICH AGENT; none asked whether one
# was needed. The ladder ran "which employee" → "hire one", so the cheapest correct
# answer — run the thing that already does this — was not on it. An org that spawns
# a reasoning agent to run a command it owns is both more expensive and LESS
# verifiable, because the exit code outranks the agent's report.
#
# The precedence is worth nothing without the total-coverage rule: a partial match
# dispatched as if complete returns a wrong answer cheaply, which is strictly worse
# than the agent hop it saved.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

check(
    "org: the dispatch CHECKPOINT weighs mechanical before it picks a node",
    "MECHANICAL BEFORE AGENTIC" in _org and "LOWEST COMPETENT NODE" in _org
    and _org.index("MECHANICAL BEFORE AGENTIC") < _org.index("LOWEST COMPETENT NODE"),
    "clause 2 must precede lowest-competent-node — a precedence rule that runs after "
    "the node is chosen has already lost the thing it was ordering",
)
check(
    "org: mechanical dispatch fires on total coverage only",
    "TOTAL COVERAGE ONLY" in _org and "partial match" in _org,
    "without it, a command that partly answers the ask returns a wrong result cheaply "
    "— worse than the agent hop it saved",
)
check(
    "org: a destructive mechanical is never auto-run",
    "destructive" in _org.lower() and "display-first" in _org,
    "clause 2 would otherwise auto-run a deploy because its coverage claim matched",
)
check(
    "org-chart-format: the Mechanicals table exists and states its zero case",
    "## Mechanicals" in _ocf and "Destructive" in _ocf and "no mechanicals" in _ocf,
    "clause 2 dispatches from this table; an absent table and an empty one must not "
    "look the same to a reader",
)

# ── The three weak points the design shipped with, closed 2026-07-31 ──────────
# 1. Coverage is matched by reading a prose cell. A positive claim reads
#    charitably; a stated BOUNDARY does not, and an unclear match resolves to an
#    agent rather than to a cheap wrong answer.
# 2. A row had no negative test while maintainers now do. `Proven` inherits one
#    where it exists and says `unproven` where it does not — which dispatches, but
#    never as a bare PASS.
# 3. Two rows claiming the same work was left to a dispatch-time tiebreak. It is a
#    defect in the TABLE; the door refuses, `index` reports.
check(
    "org: an unclear coverage match resolves to an agent, not to a guess",
    "UNCLEAR IS NOT TOTAL" in _org and "softest joint" in _org,
    "clause 2a must say what happens when totality is UNCLEAR — without it a literal "
    "reader treats plausible-but-unconfirmed as total, which is the whole risk",
)
check(
    "org-chart-format: a coverage claim states its boundary, and an empty one is unfinished",
    "Does NOT cover" in _ocf and "unfinished row" in _ocf,
    "a positive claim is read charitably by whoever matches an ask against it; the "
    "boundary is the cell that cannot be",
)
# ── A host can withdraw the capability every gate here depends on ────────────
# Found 2026-07-31 by tracing why cold readers were never spawned this session:
# an ambient instruction, delivered outside this project, suppressing subagent
# spawning. Phase C had argued the UNAVAILABLE case at length; Phase B — the
# release gate — had only PASS/FAIL/AMBIGUOUS, so "the spawn did not happen" had
# nowhere to land. Written literally the gate deadlocks; run loosely it registers
# unprobed handbooks that look released.
#
# The detection rule is the load-bearing part. The channel is unversioned and
# outside this project, so a key or flag NAME read today is renamed next release
# and the check reports success against a rename. Measure the behaviour.

# ── A marker MENTIONED is not a marker PRESENT ───────────────────────────────
# Found by the first sweep ever run. bin/baseline line-anchored its PAIRING check
# and documented exactly why — "a marker quoted inside a sentence is documentation
# describing the format, not a span opener" — while its marker TOTALS did not
# anchor. One file, one population, two answers.
#
# Measured on the target: origin_user_immutable counted 68 naive against 37
# anchored. 31 mentions, 46% inflation — and the extraction gate blocked a sweep
# that was completable, because the census it asserted against was counting prose.
# The dangerous direction is the other one: the sweep removes opener-to-closer, so
# a mention matched as an opener runs a span to the next closer and takes real
# content with it.
# ── Found by the first fixtures, 2026-07-31 ──────────────────────────────────
