    "invariant to a script, to a judgment, or to nothing",
)
check(
    "data-skills: a maintainer is released by making it fail",
    "Negative test" in ds and "released by making it fail" in ds,
    "the maintainer row must carry a negative-test cell; a validator never observed "
    "rejecting anything is indistinguishable from `exit 0`",
)
check(
    "data-skills: a maintainer detects and never repairs",
    "never repairs" in ds and "exits nonzero" in ds,
    "a maintainer that edits what it validates is a second writer of a single-owner "
    "dataset; one that exits 0 on unreadable data reports health it did not measure",
)
# The narrowing must be VISIBLE. "Authoring is descriptive" was true of everything
# authoring did until step 5 wrote a script — a rule never tested against the case
# that breaks it. Silently deleting it would be the revocation this project fails on.
check(
    "handbook: the data-skill authoring step writes maintainers, and says what narrowed",
    "run its negative test" in _hb and "narrowing of earlier wording" in _hb,
    "handbook.md § Authoring a data skill must add the maintainer step AND state that "
    "'authoring is descriptive' narrowed to the data rather than quietly disappearing",
